WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.525
Now, what the program is.

2
00:00:01.525 --> 00:00:04.816
It starts with a short charter:
the page the sponsor signs,

3
00:00:04.816 --> 00:00:09.438
and the page every later decision is
checked against: is this inside the scope we

4
00:00:09.438 --> 00:00:12.099
chartered, does it serve
one of the objectives,

5
00:00:12.099 --> 00:00:14.200
and does it move a success criterion?

6
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:17.238
The problem it sets out
to remove has four costs:

7
00:00:17.238 --> 00:00:20.743
migration risk concentrated
in hidden dependencies;

8
00:00:20.743 --> 00:00:25.027
ongoing drift between intended
and actual state; weak evidence of

9
00:00:25.027 --> 00:00:29.700
change and compliance; and a high cost
of reconciling fragmented stores.

10
00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:32.025
Against those, six objectives.

11
00:00:32.025 --> 00:00:35.602
One authoritative origin for
organizational structure,

12
00:00:35.602 --> 00:00:39.700
identity attributes and key claims,
with every other copy derived.

13
00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:43.123
Governance rebuilt explicitly,
through attributes,

14
00:00:43.123 --> 00:00:45.612
dynamic membership and scoped policy.

15
00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:48.087
Drift treated as a classified finding.

16
00:00:48.087 --> 00:00:52.227
Change in controlled waves that
start from the authoritative source,

17
00:00:52.227 --> 00:00:55.225
run under least privilege,
and close with evidence.

18
00:00:55.225 --> 00:00:58.238
Domain transformations
without rip-and-replace.

19
00:00:58.238 --> 00:01:01.000
And continuous, machine-usable evidence.

20
00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:02.650
The scope is deliberate.

21
00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:06.413
The program feeds compliance
frameworks; it doesn't replace them.

22
00:01:06.413 --> 00:01:10.046
Identity providers, network
fabrics and device managers

23
00:01:10.046 --> 00:01:13.074
stay the enforcers, and
the program governs them.

24
00:01:13.074 --> 00:01:16.263
And the adopting agency
executes its own cutover.

25
00:01:16.263 --> 00:01:18.963
An agency can adopt
the charter as written.

26
00:01:18.963 --> 00:01:23.656
The decision: the sponsor signs it,
and names go into its governance table,

27
00:01:23.656 --> 00:01:27.860
starting with the sponsor and the
steward, as Phase 0's entry work.
